From: Armada <armada@fyralabs.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Make the startup socket timeout configurable

The Legion Y700 Gen2 needs about fifty seconds before Gamescope reports its
displays, and that wait is a property of the hardware rather than cold cache
work: restricting the Vulkan ICDs changed nothing. Fifteen seconds was written
for SD-card Deck boots, so every Steam attempt on this tablet ended in
"gamescope failed" and a fallback to the desktop. Let the device profile raise
the window through ARMADA_GAMESCOPE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT.
---
--- a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
+++ b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
@@ -120,6 +120,13 @@
 fi
 if [ "${ARMADA_GAMESCOPE_USE_ROTATION_SHADER:-0}" = "1" ]; then
 	FORCE_COMPOSITION_ROTATION=1
+fi
+
+# Gamescope readiness is a fixed wait on some panels, so let the device
+# profile say how long to wait for the startup socket instead of baking
+# one number in for every device.
+if [ -n "${ARMADA_GAMESCOPE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT:-}" ]; then
+	GAMESCOPE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT="$ARMADA_GAMESCOPE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT"
 fi
 
 # Source client app specific configuration files
@@ -336,7 +343,7 @@
 $GAMESCOPECMD &
 gamescope_pid="$!"
 
-if read -r -t 15 response_x_display response_wl_display <>"$socket"; then
+if read -r -t "${GAMESCOPE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT:-15}" response_x_display response_wl_display <>"$socket"; then
 	export DISPLAY="$response_x_display"
 	export GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY="$response_wl_display"
 	# We're done!


